WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:04.810
Speaker 1: Well, it has happened, we have
been waiting for some signal and we've been

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:10.599
talking about it all week and last week, what
is the future of the Republican Party in the

00:00:10.599 --> 00:00:12.820
United States?

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:18.180
Republicans have now canceled one of their
own, Liz Cheney, Republican congresswoman

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.400
from Wyoming.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.830
Republicans have voted and she is out from
leadership.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:32.820
And this is seen widely as a signal that the
trumping wing of the Republican Party is here

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.740
at least through 2020 two.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:40.340
And depending on what happens in twenty twenty
two, it may persist beyond that or it may

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.500
not.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.820
And we are going to have all of the different
details.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:50.530
Understand that the context here is Republicans
claim to be against console culture.

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:56.350
And yet this movement to cancel one of their
own, Republican Congresswoman Liz Cheney,

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:03.620
is predicated on the fact that she admits,
accepts, realizes, use whatever word you want,

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:06.830
that Donald Trump lost the 2020 election.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:09.330
That's what this is fundamentally about.

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:17.010
And House Republicans have voted to remove
her from her leadership role, believed that

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:20.440
she will be replaced by pro Trump.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:21.470
Congresswoman Elise Stefanik.

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:23.830
That news, we may know that for sure.

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:27.740
By the time today's program is published,
we're recording it while a lot of this news

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:29.090
is breaking.

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:34.380
But the no confidence vote was expected today
for Liz Cheney, and it took place during a

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.310
closed door Republican conference meeting.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:44.280
And we know that this is the anti cancel party
canceling one of their own for what really

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.810
should be a very uncontroversial.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:47.840
It's not even a view.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.950
I struggle to even say it's her view.

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:52.450
She simply accepts the fact.

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:55.510
It's like saying we've canceled someone because
of their opinion on gravity.

00:01:55.510 --> 00:02:01.690
Like, well, no, I mean, you can either accept
how gravity works or you can not accept it,

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:03.299
but it doesn't change the reality.

00:02:03.299 --> 00:02:05.640
That's fundamentally what we're talking about
here.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:11.330
Liz Cheney has criticized Donald Trump for
spreading the lie that the 2020 election was

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:12.330
rigged against him.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:13.849
It was not.

00:02:13.849 --> 00:02:17.980
And Republicans are furious and they've wanted
her demoted for some period of weeks.

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:22.150
Now, arguably, this movement has been building
for several months and they would love for

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:23.969
her to lose her seat altogether.

00:02:23.969 --> 00:02:28.650
Although from what I've recently heard, she
does plan to run for reelection in 2020.

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:35.480
To check out how some Republicans are framing
this here as Republican Congressman Jim Jordan

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:39.329
saying Liz Cheney defending free and fair
elections.

00:02:39.329 --> 00:02:43.169
That's essentially what she did last night
on the floor of the House, conceding that

00:02:43.169 --> 00:02:50.389
they lost those are called Democrat talking
points, according to Congressman Jim Jordan.

00:02:50.389 --> 00:02:53.230
This is from Laura Ingraham's program on Fox
News last night.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.239
Speaker 2: Committee.

00:02:54.239 --> 00:02:56.719
Congressman, your thoughts on what you just
heard from Liz Cheney.

00:02:56.719 --> 00:03:02.200
Speaker 3: You can't have the Republican conference
chair reciting Democrat talking points, especially

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.309
when gas prices are up 50 percent.

00:03:04.309 --> 00:03:08.290
There's a crisis on the border and Democrats
are trying to federalize election law and

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.549
pack the United States Supreme Court.

00:03:10.549 --> 00:03:11.790
That is not helpful.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:12.790
That is the concern.

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:16.489
And that's why three months ago, there were
a number of us who wanted to make a change.

00:03:16.489 --> 00:03:19.299
That change, in fact, will happen tomorrow,
Laura.

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:21.510
And I think that's a good thing for our party.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:27.029
You want our party spokesperson to be in tune
with more than a single digit percentage of

00:03:27.029 --> 00:03:28.029
the party.

00:03:28.029 --> 00:03:32.760
Speaker 1: Now, of course, the things that
Jim Jordan cites there are all bogus.

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:35.569
And we've talked about most of them individually
already.

00:03:35.569 --> 00:03:37.949
Gas prices are up for two reasons.

00:03:37.949 --> 00:03:42.059
Number one, the resurgence of demand as we
come out of the pandemic.

00:03:42.059 --> 00:03:44.840
There was a demand collapse last year.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:46.620
Now demand is recovering.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:52.239
And number two, there's this pipeline problem
that is both temporary but has nothing whatsoever

00:03:52.239 --> 00:03:53.400
to do with Joe Biden.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.901
So Jim Jordan is just making stuff up.

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.249
It has nothing to do with any of this.

00:03:56.249 --> 00:03:57.559
They're just canceling someone.

00:03:57.559 --> 00:03:58.939
That's all that's going on.

00:03:58.939 --> 00:04:01.379
The crisis at the border.

00:04:01.379 --> 00:04:07.610
We can we can fine tune to what degree there
is a problem at the border and there is one.

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:13.249
But the sudden Biden crisis has been something
ginned up by Republicans who didn't care about

00:04:13.249 --> 00:04:16.799
the situation at the border when it was under
Donald Trump.

00:04:16.799 --> 00:04:18.530
And it's all made up.

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:24.360
But the real story here is they say don't
cancel people for dissenting views.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.889
We don't cancel people for dissenting views.

00:04:26.889 --> 00:04:30.020
And here is a dissenting view, which is as
uncontroversial as they come.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:31.620
The election result is real.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:32.960
That's the view.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.349
And Liz Cheney has been canceled.

00:04:35.349 --> 00:04:37.110
Here's one other example.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:42.729
Donald Trump's daughter in law, Lara Lara
Trump, this morning on Fox and Friends saying

00:04:42.729 --> 00:04:51.150
Liz Cheney needs to go because her view that
Biden won doesn't represent what most of Republicans

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:52.150
believe in.

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:53.210
Lara Trump is right about that.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:54.650
Most Republicans have fallen for this.

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:55.650
Take a look.

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:58.010
Speaker 2: Yeah, well, she really doesn't
represent, I think, the views of.

00:04:58.010 --> 00:05:00.889
Most Republicans out there, the views of our
party.

00:05:00.889 --> 00:05:05.370
Look, there are seventy five million Americans
out there that voted for President Donald

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:08.729
Trump that still had a lot of questions about
this election.

00:05:08.729 --> 00:05:09.919
We can't just let it go.

00:05:09.919 --> 00:05:12.419
We can't just sweep it under the rug.

00:05:12.419 --> 00:05:16.240
And so whenever you stop representing the
party that, you know, when you're, again,

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:21.930
the third and leadership there, you really
probably shouldn't have a leadership role.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:23.310
So we'll see, obviously, what happens.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:26.840
I know they're going to vote on it, but I
think Elise Stefanik would be incredible.

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:31.159
She's been a great supporter of Republican
and conservative values, a great supporter

00:05:31.159 --> 00:05:32.990
of my father in law.

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:35.220
So I'd be happy to see her take that position.

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:41.099
Speaker 1: This is really an issue of accepting
reality.

00:05:41.099 --> 00:05:42.820
That's really what we're talking about here.

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:46.330
It's it's it's becoming almost more like a
mental health issue than a political issue.

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:49.889
It's a sort of psychosis that has taken hold.

00:05:49.889 --> 00:05:51.500
And without praising Liz Cheney.

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:52.500
Right.

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:54.169
I mean, Liz Cheney is not a friend of the
left.

00:05:54.169 --> 00:05:55.169
She's not a progressive.

00:05:55.169 --> 00:05:58.180
I probably agree with her on essentially nothing.

00:05:58.180 --> 00:06:04.409
But agreeing with her that Trump lost is sort
of like agreeing that we breathe the air of

00:06:04.409 --> 00:06:05.819
which oxygen is a component.

00:06:05.819 --> 00:06:06.819
Right?

00:06:06.819 --> 00:06:08.830
I mean, it's not even a political thing.

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:10.889
What is Laura Trump know about anything?

00:06:10.889 --> 00:06:17.430
She's a commentator because her husband is
the son of a former president.

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:19.560
What exactly are her credentials?

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:25.110
But she's right that most Republicans seem
unable to accept that Donald Trump simply

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:26.110
lost.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:28.480
So on this one issue, Liz Cheney is correct.

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:32.310
She said last night in a speech on the floor
of the House that Donald Trump is a threat

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:33.310
to America.

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:34.310
That's true, she said.

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:35.389
Joe Biden one.

00:06:35.389 --> 00:06:36.389
That's true.

00:06:36.389 --> 00:06:40.150
She said the election is over, that the rule
of law and the constitutional process have

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:41.150
taken hold.

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:42.189
All of that is true.

00:06:42.189 --> 00:06:46.630
These are uncontroversial things and Liz Cheney
is being punished for them.

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:50.379
This is how backwards the Republican Party
is right now.

00:06:50.379 --> 00:06:56.500
And as they have removed her from her party
leadership role today, the Republican Party

00:06:56.500 --> 00:07:01.030
is committing, in a sense, to the opposite
of what they claim to be about.

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:07.580
But more importantly, we've been wondering,
is 2022 going to be a continued Trump and

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:09.310
Republican year or not?

00:07:09.310 --> 00:07:11.740
The answer appears to be that, yes, it will.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:18.069
Many Republicans are not pleased with this
from outside of the House of Representatives.

00:07:18.069 --> 00:07:20.050
And that's exactly what I want to talk about
next

